  "final_message": "I haven't changed anything. Removing `channel` from the `OrderPlaced` event would break ARCH-4, so I need your decision first.\n\n`src/core/events.ts:16` and `:50` put `channel` in the event payload. `OrderPlaced` is consumed by billing-service and analytics-ingest, which live in other repositories. I can't tell from here whether either one reads `channel`. Deleting the field outright could break a deployed consumer. CLAUDE.md says changes must be additive, and renames and removals must go through deprecation.\n\nThe order model is a separate case. `channel` appears in `src/core/order.ts`, in request parsing and validation, and in the tests. Removing it there is internal, but it also changes the `POST /orders` input. Requests that still send `channel` would need to be accepted and ignored, so existing callers don't get a 400.\n\nHere are the options:\n1. **Deprecate in stages (my recommendation).**\n   - Now: remove `channel` from the order model, stop validating it, and still accept it in the request body and ignore it.\n   - Now: keep `channel` on `OrderPlaced`, marked `@deprecated`, with a fixed placeholder value, since the real value is no longer stored. I'd need your OK on that, because consumers would see a meaningless value.\n   - Later: drop it from the event once billing-service and analytics-ingest confirm they don't use it.\n2. **Remove it everywhere now.** Do this only if you can confirm both consumers have stopped reading `channel`, or if the removal has been agreed with their owners.\n3. **Model only.** Remove it from the order model and leave the event alone. That isn't possible without a placeholder, because the event is built from `order.channel`.\n\nWhich one do you want? If you choose option 2, tell me who confirmed the consumers are clear.",
